---
title: A recipe search, from click to page
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Visitor
    participant B as Chrome
    participant A as Apache
    participant L as Laravel<br/>(PHP-FPM)
    participant S as RecipeSearch
    participant D as MariaDB

    U->>B: types "pizza", sorts by "Quickest"
    B->>A: GET /recipes?q=pizza&sort=quickest
    A->>L: no such file, so index.php (FastCGI)
    L->>L: middleware: session, CSRF token, security headers
    L->>S: RecipeController@index hands over the query string
    S->>S: drop unknown filters, match the sort against SORTS
    S->>D: queries with bound parameters, related data eager-loaded
    D-->>S: rows for page 1 (up to 12 recipes) and the total
    S-->>L: paginated recipes
    L->>L: render recipes/index.blade.php, nonce in the CSP
    L-->>A: HTML (Cache-Control: no-cache, private)
    A-->>B: HTML, gzip-compressed
    B->>A: CSS, JavaScript, fonts, visible photos
    A-->>B: static files, cached for a year (photos a week)
    Note over B,A: Photos further down load only when scrolled to,<br/>and a later visit takes the static files from the cache
